<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna tailcontract: a single-function decompile of a tail-calling thunk.

    gcc -O2 -fno-pic -no-pie of
        int target(int a, int *b) { if (b) *b = a; sink = a; return a * 3 + 1; }
        int thunk(int a) { return target(a, 0); }          // xor esi,esi; jmp target
        int helper(int a, int b, int c) { sink = b; return a + b * c; }
        int pass(int a, int b, int c) { return helper(a, b + 1, c); }  // add esi,1; jmp helper
    Decompiled alone, thunk dropped the tail call's result (nothing in it reads
    RAX) and pass dropped `c`, which it forwards in EDX untouched.  With the
    option on the drive first decompiles each tail-called callee and states its
    recovered prototype, as decompile-all's callee-first order does.

    Stage: P4 callee prototype contract, option tailcontract off|on.  Pass 1
    (off) pins the bug, pass 2 (on, the default) pins the fix.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000">
f30f1efae9670000000f1f8000000000f30f1efa4885f67402893e893ddf1f00008d447f01c3662e0f1f840000000000f30f1efa31f6ebd80f1f840000000000f30f1efa8935b61f00000faff28d043ec30f1f400066662e0f1f840000000000f30f1efa83c601ebd70f1f8000000000f30f1efae8b7ffffffba03000000be0200000089c1e8d6ffffff8d440101c3
</bytechunk>
